# Per-model encoder geometry for unifi_avclient_go.
#
# The HIGH channel's real width/height are a property of the physical encoder,
# not of the declared catalog model, so the client reads them from here instead
# of carrying a model table in the binary. That is what keeps one universal
# client correct on every model -- including models introduced after the client
# was built -- with per-model facts living next to that model's bring-up.
#
# Format, one model per line, whitespace-separated; '#' starts a comment:
#
#     <model_suffix> <high_width> <high_height>
#
# A model with no line here falls back to the y623-class 2304x1296. Values are
# verified by decoding a real SPS NAL from that model's encoder output.
#
# Keep this list additive and minimal: a fix for one model must not silently
# change another. Do not add a model until its geometry has actually been
# measured on that hardware.
y623    2304 1296
h52ga   1920 1080
y291ga  1920 1080
# r35gb is GC2053-class and is expected to be 1920x1080, but is deliberately
# left unlisted: correcting it is an r35gb change and must be verified/deployed
# as such, not ride along with another model's bring-up. Uncomment after it has
# been confirmed from that camera's own SPS.
#r35gb  1920 1080
